30,2,,status,Toshio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
31,2,,status,Rin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
32,2,,status,Shion,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
33,2,,status,Mizuki,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Yumi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Rin,,"Wow, I found some really important stuff! It takes a few minutes every single morning just to get set up upstairs, and those unplanned shuffles are a total mess! They last for two whole weeks! That's way too long!","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"The cost of inefficiency is higher than you think. We are billed by area, not headcount, meaning empty space is a waste. Furthermore, every single desk move incurs a specific facility charge. We cannot afford a trial-and-error approach.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"The data confirms my suspicions. There is a significant noise difference between the corridor and the window side. Also, our arrival times vary wildly, meaning any ""first-come"" logic for the better seats is inherently unfair.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shion,,"It's interesting that you mention fairness, Mizuki. The real issue is that our equipment requires days of precise adjustment to be comfortable. If we shuffle seats carelessly, we're essentially resetting our physical well-being to zero.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"I found something so interesting! Our new teammates learned so much just by overhearing us! Also, the survey shows people really miss the sunlight. I want us to make sure everyone gets some light and feels included!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Rin,,"Two weeks of boxes is like a forever-mess! If we pick a layout that's too stiff, we'll just end up in that chaos again. We need something that's easy to change but doesn't waste our mornings!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"Easy to change is a luxury we cannot afford. With a per-desk charge for every move and a monthly bill for unused area, we must commit to a single, optimized layout from the start.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"If we commit to one layout, we must be honest about the trade-offs. The window side is quieter and brighter, while the corridor is noisy. We can't just hope for the best; we need a clear rule for who sits where.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shion,,"A ""clear rule"" is just another way of ignoring individual needs. If we prioritize a rigid system over the time it takes to actually calibrate a workstation, we're just choosing a different kind of inefficiency.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"I understand everyone's worries! But if we're too rigid, we might miss out on those happy, accidental conversations that help new people feel welcome. Can we find a way to balance the budget and the sunlight?","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Rin,,"But if we spend all our time worrying about rules and money, we'll forget to be happy! We need a plan that's fast to set up and doesn't make us move boxes for two weeks!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"Happiness does not pay the bills, Rin. If we ignore the financial reality, we risk a budget shortfall that could affect us all. We need a layout that maximizes our paid area without incurring repeated facility charges.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"Budget and happiness aren't mutually exclusive, but silence on the ""bad"" seats is a problem. Since the window side is objectively better, we should decide now who takes the noisy corridor spots to avoid resentment.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shion,,"Resentment is a psychological byproduct; physical strain is a biological reality. If we ignore the fact that it takes days to settle into a desk, we're just rearranging who suffers. Comfort isn't a luxury—it's the baseline for productivity.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"I totally get that! We should definitely make sure everyone is comfortable. But maybe we can use that ""bad"" noise to our advantage? If we sit closer, we can help each other and learn together!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Rin,,"I don't think noise is a good way to learn! But we have to be careful. If we pick a layout that's too hard to change, we'll be stuck in a mess for weeks! Let's pick something simple!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Toshio,,"Simplicity is only valuable if it is sustainable. A ""simple"" plan that requires frequent adjustments will drain our budget through repeated facility charges. We must prioritize a layout that is final and cost-effective.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Mizuki,,"If we want a final, cost-effective layout, we must address the inequality of the space. Let's be transparent: some seats are worse than others. We need a fair method to assign them, rather than leaving it to chance.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shion,,"Transparency is a start, but fairness isn't about who gets the ""bad"" seat; it's about acknowledging that once we sit, we stay. Let's stop treating desks like interchangeable tiles and start treating them like tools.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Yumi,,"I agree! Our desks are tools for our work and our friendships! Let's find a way to give everyone sunlight and comfort, while keeping us close enough to support each other. I'm sure we can find a perfect balance!","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,,status,Toshio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
56,3,,status,Rin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
