58,3,,status,Mizuki,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
59,3,,status,Yumi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
60,3,1,talk,Rin,,"Option A sounds like a nightmare! I found out that setting up takes forever every morning, and we'd have to do that every single day? No way! I vote for Option C!","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"Option A is financially reckless due to the lack of optimization, and Option B is impossible given the per-desk facility charges for every move. Option C is the only sustainable choice. I vote for Option C.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Mizuki,,"Option A is unfair because early arrivals always get the best seats. Option B is too disruptive. Option C is the most logical, provided we are honest and fair about who gets the noisy seats. I vote for Option C.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shion,,Option A is a disaster for anyone who values their body; resetting a workstation daily is physically impossible. Option B is just a scheduled cycle of discomfort. Option C is the only logical choice. I vote for Option C.,"{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Yumi,,"I'm a bit sad that we can't move around, but I agree! Option C lets us stay close and support each other without the stress of moving boxes. I vote for Option C too!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Rin,,"Wait, does everyone really agree? I'm just so relieved we aren't doing the daily setup thing! It would have eaten up all my free time between meetings! Option C is definitely the winner!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Toshio,,The consensus is clear. Option C minimizes unnecessary facility costs and prevents the waste of our paid floor area. It is the only choice that aligns with our financial and operational constraints.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Mizuki,,"Since we've all agreed on Option C, we must now decide how to assign the seats. Let's not leave the noisy corridor spots to chance or habit; we should discuss a fair way to allocate them.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shion,,"Let's not overcomplicate it. Since we've agreed on fixed desks, the priority should be stability. Once we are placed, we stay. That is the only way to ensure the physical calibration of our workstations actually lasts.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Yumi,,"I agree! Stability is great, but let's make sure we place people who love to chat and help each other side-by-side. That way, we can keep that wonderful team spirit alive every single day!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Rin,,"I'll help with the chatting part! As long as we don't have to move our stuff every two weeks or every morning, I'm super happy! Let's just make sure the plan is easy to understand!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"As long as the plan is finalized and documented, it will be easy to understand. We have avoided the financial pitfalls of the other options. Let us proceed with Option C.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Mizuki,,"I'm glad we're aligned on the option, but we can't ignore the noise data. Let's agree now that the corridor seats are the ""hard"" spots, and decide together who takes them so no one feels slighted.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shion,,"The ""hard"" spots are only a problem if we treat them as a punishment. Let's just assign them and move on. The real victory here is that we've finally prioritized stability over chaos.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Yumi,,"I think we can make the ""hard"" spots feel special too! Maybe we can put the most helpful people there to greet everyone? Let's just make sure we're all happy with our neighbors!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Rin,,"That sounds like a great idea, Yumi! Let's make the corridor the ""Welcome Zone""! I'm so glad we're doing this. I officially vote for Option C! Let's go make our new desks awesome!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Toshio,,My vote is for Option C. It is the only choice that ensures financial stability and prevents wasteful spending on repeated facility charges. We have reached a practical conclusion.,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Mizuki,,"I vote for Option C. While I'm glad we've reached a consensus, I insist that we explicitly discuss the seat assignments next to ensure the distribution of the noisy spots is fair.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Shion,,"I vote for Option C. It is the only choice that respects the physical reality of our work. Now that we have stability, we can finally focus on the actual comfort of our seats.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Yumi,,I vote for Option C too! I'm so happy we all agree. Let's make sure we sit in a way that keeps us all connected and smiling! I can't wait to start!,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
